      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t actually block -- instead, it returns right away. If le_rand hasn\u0027t returned by the time it runs, it will just return Err(_) and you unwrap below will crash.\n\nShove this into a tokio::block_on with a timeout:\n```\nconst SUSPEND_TIMEOUT \u003d 2000;\nlet result \u003d tokio::block_on(async move {\n  match tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_millis(SUSPEND_TIMEOUT), c.recv()).await {\n    Ok(recv) \u003d\u003e match recv {\n      Ok(rand_value) \u003d\u003e rand_value !\u003d 0,\n      Err(_) \u003d\u003e false,\n    },\n    // Timeout\n    Err(_) \u003d\u003e false,\n  }\n});\n\nif result {\n  // Suspend ready\n} else {\n  // Bad suspend state. What do you do if le_rand times out or le_rand returns 0?\n  // To try to be resilient, maybe you just log it and just emit suspend ready\n  // anyway?\n}\n```",
